Assume **x86-64 Linux, gcc, little-endian, `int` = 4 bytes, pointer = 8 bytes.**

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    int n = 4, k = 1;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        printf("%*s", n - i, "");
        for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++)
            printf("%d", k++ % 10);
        printf(" %d %d\n", k, k++);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

Type the exact output, or choose **Undefined Behavior** / **Compile Error**.

